* ZK proof systems
** The one engine
*** Schwartz-Zippel: d / |F| error
*** Low-degree extension: table -> polynomial
*** Every system is a polynomial identity test

** Arithmetisation
*** R1CS: (Az) o (Bz) = Cz
**** Spartan, Marlin, Nova
*** QAP: A(X)B(X) - C(X) = H(X)Z(X)
**** Pinocchio, Groth16
*** AIR: trace + transition constraints
**** STARK

** Information-theoretic core
*** Sum-check protocol
**** GKR, Spartan
*** Interactive oracle proofs (IOP)
*** Algebraic holographic proofs (AHP)
**** Marlin's compiler recipe

** Commitment layer
*** KZG pairing-based, constant size
**** Sonic, Marlin
*** Pedersen + inner product argument
**** Bulletproofs, Halo, Spartan, Nova
*** Merkle + FRI, hash only
**** STARK

** Setup spectrum
*** Per-circuit SRS: Pinocchio, Groth16
*** Universal and updatable SRS: Sonic, Marlin
*** Transparent, no setup: STARK, Bulletproofs, Halo, Spartan

** Making it non-interactive
*** Fiat-Shamir: r = H(transcript)
*** Random oracle model
*** Transcript binding is where systems break

** Security notions
*** Soundness vs knowledge soundness
*** Extractor defines "knows a witness"
*** Simulator defines zero knowledge
*** Goldreich-Krawczyk: composition has limits

** Recursion
*** Halo: defer the linear check, amortise
*** Nova: fold two R1CS instances into one
*** Both give IVC with constant-size proofs

** Application
*** Zerocash: commitments, nullifiers, Merkle membership
*** The proof hides origin, destination and amount
@endmindmap
